  "verbalization": "Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside appears to interact with Thioredoxin, mitochondrial through a shared target of the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This subunit is a common target for multiple compounds, including Diplotrin A, Phorone, and Flavipin, all of which are linked to Thioredoxin, mitochondrial. The evidence suggests a potential pathway where Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside may modulate the proteasome complex, thereby influencing the activity of Thioredoxin, mitochondrial. The presence of multiple compounds targeting the same subunit implies a possible mechanism of action involving proteasome regulation, which could indirectly affect Thioredoxin activity. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of the 26S proteasome in mediating the interaction between Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside and Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, suggesting a broader functional relationship that warrants further investigation.",
